content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-111 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-21100",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 4.2 mm/s is in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation') of the HF-300 severity chart, so it is below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C limit ('Restricted - plan maintenance'). It is only 0.3 mm/s below that limit. The manual says to classify the highest reading taken on either bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature 74 C is above the 70 C normal limit. It is below the 80 C alarm and the 90 C trip, so it is elevated but not at alarm. Temperatures are measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Grinding noise from the non-drive-end bearing (6310-C3, HF3-510) is a bearing-wear symptom. The manual requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either shows noise or high temperature, and both apply here.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "'Seal is dry': the seal must never run dry, and it is flushed by a Plan 11 flush from the pump discharge. If 'dry' means the seal faces are running without flush, this breaches a documented limit. If it only means there is no leakage, it is normal. The report does not say which.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Overall, the readings are not past any documented stop limit: vibration is not in Zone D and temperature is below the 90 C trip. However, the noise and above-normal temperature require planned bearing replacement, so the job is set as P2.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Non-drive-end bearing wear. This fits the grinding noise, the elevated housing temperature and the rising vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing. It is a listed cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation. These are listed causes of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Confirm with operations what 'seal is dry' means. If the seal is running without Plan 11 flush, stop the pump immediately, because the seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, re-measure vibration on both bearing housings in mm/s RMS. Classify the highest reading against Figure 3, and stop the pump if it reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s). Record the housing temperatures and stop the pump at 90 C (trip).",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the grease quantity on both bearings to rule out over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair: non-drive-end 6310-C3 (HF3-510) and drive-end 6312-C3 (HF3-512).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, inspect the impeller for damage or imbalance. Inspect the mechanical seal faces and the shaft sleeve for scoring. Replace seal HF3-450 if the faces are worn or cracked, or if the seal has run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Refit the assembly with a new casing gasket HF3-120. Tighten all fasteners to the values in Manual Table 5. The Table 5 values are not in the evidence provided, so obtain them before starting. Do not use the 30 Nm gland torque from SB-2026-014.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align the shaft. The tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restarting, confirm the Plan 11 seal flush is in place. After restart, re-check vibration (target Zone A/B, below 4.5 mm/s) and housing temperature (normal up to 70 C).",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as a pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replace as a pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever the casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type. Contingency: fit only if inspection shows damage or the seal has run dry. This is the correct seal for serials below HF3-22000.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency: fit only if inspection finds scoring.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before any dismantling.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the seal dry. Verify the Plan 11 flush from the discharge before any run or restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump if vibration enters Zone D (7.1 mm/s or above) or housing temperature reaches the 90 C trip. Treat 80 C as an alarm.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h with 2 technicians. Possible overlap with the bearing job (shared back pull-out) is not stated, so do not assume a reduction.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "SB-2026-014 (14 March 2026) supersedes seal HF3-450 with HF3-450B, sets a 30 Nm gland torque and sets a 0.1 mm sleeve scoring limit. It applies only to serial HF3-22000 and above. P-111 is serial HF3-21100, which is below that range. The bulletin itself says pumps below HF3-22000 continue to use HF3-450 and Manual Table 5. Therefore use the manual's part HF3-450 and Table 5 torques, not HF3-450B or 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Manual Table 5 fastener torque values, including the seal gland torque for HF3-450, are not in the evidence provided. Obtain them before reassembly.",
    "Does 'seal is dry' mean no leakage (normal), or that the seal is running without Plan 11 flush (stop condition)?",
    "Was the 4.2 mm/s reading in mm/s RMS, which housing was it taken on, and is it the highest of the two housings?",
    "Which housing gave the 74 C reading, and what are the readings on each housing?",
    "The manual gives no sleeve scoring acceptance limit for serials below HF3-22000. The 0.1 mm limit applies only to bearings-bulletin serials HF3-22000 and above.",
    "The manual gives no detailed bearing replacement steps, bearing fitting method, grease type or grease quantity.",
    "The evidence does not cover site lockout/isolation procedure, PPE or permit requirements.",
    "Whether a cavitation/NPSH check is warranted, given the suction conditions are unknown."
  ]
}
